<title>UK: Czech Export Bank to launch debut Eurobond.</title>
<headline>Czech Export Bank to launch debut Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech Export Bank has won shareholder approval for its debut Eurobond issue, J.P. Morgan said on Thursday as lead manager. The bond will have a statutory state guarantee.  </p>
<p>&quot;Our decision to issue a Eurobond reflects the continued confidence in the Czech economy and the growing prospects for our domestic policy,&quot; said CEB director Tomas Revesz.</p>
<p>J.P. Morgan will also act as a rating advisor for the CEB.</p>
<p>The Czech Republic is rated Baa1/A.</p>
<p>Revesz said the CEB was created to establish a domestic export promotion policy following the country's transformation to a market economy.</p>
<p>-- Dan Lalor, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
